\pard\plain \sa240\sb240\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0 T}{\f1\fs24\b0 ardigrades are small (<1 mm) aquatic ecdysozoans that occupy a distinct phylum, Tardigrada. This controversial phylogenetic positioning provides important insights into the evolution of arthropods and nematodes}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref1"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\super ,}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref2"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f1\fs24\b0 . Limno-terrestrial tardigrades can withstand almost complete desiccation through a mechanism called anhydrobiosis}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref3"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 3}}{\f1\fs24\b0\super ,}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref4"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 4}}{\f1\fs24\b0 , and tardigrades can survive extreme environments, including extreme temperature}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref5"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 5}}{\f1\fs24\b0 , pressure}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref6"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 6}}{\f1\fs24\b0\super ,}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref7"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 7}}{\f1\fs24\b0 , radiation}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref8"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 8}}{\f1\fs24\b0\super ,\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8203\'3F}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref9"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 9}}{\f1\fs24\b0\super ,\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8203\'3F}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref10"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 0}{\f1\fs24\b0 , and even exposure to the vacuum of space}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref11"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}{\f1\fs24\b0 . Although it is a weak anhydrobiote}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref12"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}{\f1\fs24\b0 , }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 Hypsibius dujardini}{\f1\fs24\b0  is a model tardigrade due to its ease of culturing}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref13"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 3}{\f1\fs24\b0 , transparent body color that is suited for developmental biology studies, and its feasibility for RNA interference-based genetic studies}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref14"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 4}{\f1\fs24\b0 .}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0 Recently, Boothby }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f1\fs24\b0  reported the sequencing of }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 H. dujardini}{\f1\fs24\b0  and demonstrated that as many as 17.5% of the genes of this organism may have been acquired through horizontal gene transfer (HGT) and that these foreign origin genes may be the key to their extremotolerance}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref15"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 5}{\f1\fs24\b0 . However, the anhydrobiotic capabilities of }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 H. dujardini}{\f1\fs24\b0  are limited compared with those of other terrestrial tardigrades}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref12"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}{\f1\fs24\b0 , and the non-axenic nature of tardigrade culture is prone to contamination, especially in light of the unusually large size of assembly (212.3 Mb) compared with previous estimates}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref13"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 3}{\f1\fs24\b0 . Hence, a calculation of the HGT rate requires comprehensive experimental evidence and careful data screening. Three research groups have provided evidence demonstrating that the HGT candidates presented by Boothby }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f1\fs24\b0  were, in fact, mostly contaminant artifacts. Delmont and Eren employed metagenomics approaches and analyzed multiple DNA and RNA libraries, and Bemm }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f1\fs24\b0  filtered Moleculo reads by k-mer frequencies, to identify contamination (including near-complete bacterial genomes) and effectively removed it from the assembly}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref16"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 6}{\f1\fs24\b0\super ,}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref17"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 7}{\f1\fs24\b0 . Koutsovoulos }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f1\fs24\b0  presented a thorough comparison using an independently sequenced assembly of the same strain of }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 H. dujardini}{\f1\fs24\b0  and found no evidence of extensive HGT in this species}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref18"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 8}{\f1\fs24\b0 .}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0 We have also been studying the same strain, but with an ultra-low input sequencing approach. Tardigrades are small animals, mostly in the range of several hundred micrometers in length and comprising approximately one thousand cells, with only several hundred picograms of DNA per individual. Therefore, naive approaches require thousands of animals to extract sufficient DNA or RNA for the construction of libraries for high-throughput sequencing; the collection of that many animals from a non-axenic culture is inherently prone to contamination. Such contamination can be screened after assembly using bioinformatics and metagenomic approaches but would ideally be minimized in the library preparation steps. To this end, we employed an ultra-low input methodology to sequence a single individual of }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 H. dujardini}{\f1\fs24\b0  to minimize contamination and provided supporting evidence that there is no extensive HGT}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref19"}{\fldrslt\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}}{\f1\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 9}{\f1\fs24\b0 . Here, we describe the details of our sequencing data and the ultra-low input library preparation methodologies. Although we also describe a series of single individual mRNA-Seq data in this work, due to the low reproducibility in some of the samples, we provide these data sets as supporting materials to possibly identify tardigrade-specific genes. Therefore, the rest of this descriptor is predominantly focused on the genome sequencing, reproducibility of which was confirmed by replications.}
